<%# How to use the box, revealed on hover — and on focus, so it is reachable by
    keyboard and on touch, where hover does not exist.

    It earns its place because the grammar REFUSES what it does not understand
    rather than falling back to a substring search. A refusal you cannot act on is
    a dead end, so the vocabulary has to be one hover away from the box that needs
    it. Every example below is copy-pasteable as written.

    No JS: CSS :hover / :focus-within only. A popover that needs a script is a
    popover that stops opening the day a nonce slips. %>
<% keys = local_assigns.fetch(:keys, RoundhouseUi::FilterQuery::KEYS) %>
<div class="rh-help">
  <button type="button" aria-label="How to search" aria-describedby="rh-help-panel">?</button>
  <div class="rh-help-panel" id="rh-help-panel" role="tooltip">
    <h4>Filters narrow. Text searches.</h4>
    <dl>
      <% if keys.include?("class") %><dt>class=</dt><dd>exact job class — <code>class=Billing::SyncWorker</code></dd><% end %>
      <% if keys.include?("error") %><dt>error=</dt><dd>exact error class — <code>error=Timeout::Error</code></dd><% end %>
      <% if keys.include?("queue") %><dt>queue=</dt><dd>exact queue name — <code>queue=default</code></dd><% end %>
      <% if RoundhouseUi.job_tags && keys.include?("tag") %>
        <dt>tag=</dt><dd>a declared tag, as <code>key:value</code> — <code>tag=squad:core</code></dd>
      <% end %>
      <dt>anything else</dt><dd>substring, across class, jid, error message and redacted arguments</dd>
    </dl>
    <dl style="margin-top:9px">
      <dt>%</dt><dd>wildcard — <code>class=Roundhouse%</code>, <code>class=%Worker</code>, <code>class=%oundhouse%</code></dd>
    </dl>
    <p class="rh-help-note">
      Combine them: <code>error=KeyError queue=ai stripe</code> means that error, on
      that queue, mentioning “stripe”. Without a <code>%</code> a filter matches
      <strong>exactly</strong>, so <code>queue=default</code> never also selects
      <code>default_low</code>. <code>_</code> is a literal, not a wildcard. Quote
      values with spaces: <code>error="Net::ReadTimeout with body"</code>. For text
      that looks like a filter, use <code>text="account_id=1234"</code>.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
